1 OCCU Lensmann og eier av Grinder gård i Grue
1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  Even Sjønnesen Grinder
2 CONT
2 CONT GRINDERBYGD--GRINDER: He was a sheriff in the district, and from his time Grinder was a sheriff’s station [literal translation: sheriff’s farm] for a long time. Even’s wife was Berte Arnesdtr, and they had four sons and two daught
2 CONC ers. Two of the sons we hear about further, and the third son was Siver (Sjur), who was marred to a widow of Rolstad in Brandval and lived there. The fourth son was Kolbjørn and he went to Øyen in Odal--he died early, but left a s
2 CONC on, Gunnar Øyen, who was owner of 3 skinn in Grinder. Of Even Grinder’s two daughters, Guro was married to Tove Sæta, and Marte to Torkjel Kjelsen Åsnes, son of Kjel Berger in Grue. Even Grinder was a well-to-do man, who along wit
2 CONC h his own farm owned farms and farm shares in both Grue and the neighboring districts. He died about 1649, but Berte lived for many years after him.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Lensmann og eier av Grinder gård i Grue Kilde; http://www.k-h-andresen.dk/slaegt/slaegt_niveau2/slaegt_niveau3/slaegt_niveau4/slaegt_niveau5/slaegt_niveau6/slaegt_niveau7/henrik1024_101_104.html -----------------------------------
2 CONC -------------------------------------------------------------------
