1 NOTE Halvor acquired the Ørje waterfalls sawmill once owned by his great
2 CONT grandfather Mogens Svendsen Lie. This was about 1750. In the years 1754-56
2 CONT there were no other sawmills in Aremark Parish and he made lumber for other
2 CONT farmers in Aremark for building and repair houses. He was fined about 221
2 CONT riksdalers and in 1758 he wrote a letter to King Fredrik V and asked to be
2 CONT excused from the fine. The fine was suspended but he could no longer make
2 CONT lumber for other farmers.
