2 CONT ==[https://start.varmlandsrotter.se/varmlandsanor/artiklar/1999_1/ A Major Property Owner in Värmland and Dalsland, By Lennart Paulsson]
2 CONT
2 CONT Margareta Persdotter was a Large landowner in Värmland and Dalsland. She inherited salvation property in Steneby parish on Dal after her mother Karin Andersdotter. After the death of her father Per Larsson's "Little Per", she also
2 CONC  inherited the farm estate Bro in Värmland, where she and her husband Nils Månsson Roos are believed to have lived from 1579. After the death of her husband in 1603, Margareta ruled and placed her own domains alone. Only in Steneb
2 CONC y under the Dingelvik farm she had 12 saviors. It was not only in Steneby that she owned properties. According to a protocol from 1619, she owned the entire Sund's farm in the parish of Nössemarks on Dal as well as several salvati
2 CONC on homes in Värmland. Margareta Persdotter died childless in Bro around 1629 and as the closest heir, Elin Jacobsdotter of rider champion Lennart Persson Svenske.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to a protocol from 1619, the entire Sunds farm was owned by Margareta Pedersdotter on Bro. She was probably married to a Pär Nilsson in Bro. He then owned Bro's farm and several other homes in Värmland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Already in this quote I see an error. Margareta was not married to Pär Nilsson but to Nils Månsson Roos. In addition, Margareta died childless and had no breast wings.
2 CONT
2 CONT The next quote reads: Pär Nilsson and Maret Nilsdotter were probably full siblings. Maret inherited his mother's ownership in Sund and had it until 1623.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1623, Maret Nilsdotter sold his ownership to Björn Nilsson in Sund. I believe that this heritage castle was sold within the family and can reasonably assume that Björn was the brother of Maret and Pär.
2 CONT
2 CONT If I can believe without having any evidence, then Maret, Pär and Björn were children of Nils Månsson Roos in a previous marriage and in this way Maret and Björn may have inherited the property in Sund in Nössemark while Nils inhe
2 CONC rited in Bro. For several years I have tried to clarify this for several years, but each time I have to give up. Maybe someone can help me figure this out, I'm grateful to have a relationship with both Margareta Persdotter and Mar
2 CONC et Nilsdotter and Björn Nilsson. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The following statement shows what I know about Margareta Persdotter:
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margareta Persdotter'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Large landowner in Värmland and Dalsland. She inherited freehold property in Steneby parish on Dal from her mother Karin Andersdotter. After the death of her father Per Larsson's "Little Per", she also inherited the Bro manor in V
2 CONC ärmland, where she and her husband Nils Månsson Roos are said to have stayed from 1579. After her husband's death in 1603, Margareta ruled and ruled alone over her domains. In Steneby alone under the Dingelvik estate, she had 12 r
2 CONC escue homes. It was not only in Steneby that she owned properties. According to a protocol from 1619, she owned the entire Sund farm in the parish of Nössemark in Dal, as well as a number of salvation homes in Värmland. Margareta 
2 CONC Persdotter died childless in Bro around 1629 and Elin Jacobsdotter Snakeborg Bååt, wife of master rider Lennart Persson Svenske, registered as the nearest heir.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Nils Månsson Roos'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Margareta Persdotter's husband Nils Månsson Roos, like his son, belonged to the cavalry of his father Karl IX. Died in 1603 in Charles IX's campaign in Livonia. He was the son of Måns Knutsson Roos of Hjelmsäter. Belonged to Charl
2 CONC es IX's horsemen and sat on the lordly seat of Blolmberg in Västergötland. Married to Christina Gregorsdotter.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Per Larsson (Little)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Margareta Persdotter's father Per Larsson  was a bailiff based at the Bro manor in Värmland. Born in 1522 in Östbro, Bro and died there in 1577. Married to Karin Andersdotter, died in 1576.
2 CONT
